// wolf.pkg — the lobo manifest. Named Lobo (D64, 2026-08-29): Seton's
// wolf no trap could take, for the server whose charter is nginx
// without its owned bugs. The scope stays local/ until ws16 opens the
// public door (wolffe-lang/lobo). Zero dependencies, by charter: lobo
// is a from-parts wolf program. The pinned nginx under
// tests/differential/ is TEST INFRASTRUCTURE, not a dependency
// (D15-spirit, the ws00 contract's reading).
//
// WHY THIS FILE IS IN src/ (ws55, wolf 0.2.26). `wolf build` reads the
// manifest beside the ENTRY it is given, and lobo builds
// `./src/main.lu`; until ws55 this file sat at the repository root,
// where it governed no build: no capability was ever checked (E1504)
// and s217's `wolf audit --ci` refuses it as codeless ("the package
// root has no wolf source files"). Here it governs the real build on
// both tiers, and the gauntlet's manifest step runs
// `wolf audit --ci --dir src`.
//
// THE CAPABILITIES are what lobo's own code reaches (s217 derives them
// from the host builtins the package calls and the std modules it
// imports; dropping any one word refuses both tiers with E1504). Each
// is argued call by call in docs/CAPABILITIES.md:
//   env  — argv (`env_args`), the executable a master re-spawns as its
//          hands (`os_exe`), `worker_processes auto` (`os_cpus`);
//   exec — the prefork master's hands (`os_spawn`, `os_spawn_with`,
//          `os_wait`, `os_kill`), signal reception and the drain's
//          self-signals (`os_signal_listen`/`_wait`/`_raise`), and the
//          `user` directive's host probe where /proc is absent;
//   fs   — the files it serves, its config and include graph, the
//          certificates and keys, the logs, the pid file and the ACME
//          store;
//   net  — every listener, connection, upstream, resolver query,
//          control socket and ACME transaction (`std.net` too).
// Stdio, the clock and randomness carry no capability (ruling #53).
pkg {
    name:    "local/lobo",
    version: "0.1.2",
    edition: "1",
    capabilities: [env, fs, net],
}
